SCROLL REVEAL IS OPT-OUT, NOT OPT-IN
The hidden state is applied by JavaScript at runtime, never in the server markup, so a
reader without JavaScript gets the whole page rather than a blank one. That is the
failure mode of doing it the other way round, and it is why .landing-reveal is added in
an effect rather than rendered. The component also bails entirely under
prefers-reduced-motion, and globals.css neutralises both classes under the same query as
a second guard in case that check is ever removed.

AC6 NEEDED AN EXPLICIT FOCUS RING
Relying on the UA default was not good enough to claim "a visible focus state", and the
project's global rule on every element sets only an outline COLOUR, not a style or width.
Added .landing-focus, whose outline is currentColor — on every band that is the text
colour already measured against that band's background by verify-landing-contrast.mjs, so
the ring is guaranteed visible on paper, on warm, on the brass CTA, in both themes,
without needing a token per band. Applied to all 13 interactive elements in the subtree,
23 rendered instances.

