A DEV-SERVER TRAP WORTH RECORDING
The focus ring appeared not to work: :focus-visible matched, the class was present, but
the computed outline was Chrome's default "auto 1px". The rule was absent from the CSSOM
entirely. It WAS in the production CSS. The dev server on :3000 was serving stale CSS and
did not pick up globals.css changes even after touching the file. All remaining
verification was done against next start on :3100. Anyone debugging landing styles should
confirm they are not looking at stale dev CSS before believing a rule does not apply.

